<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.5.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01820</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.5.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>0a00d4b8-81af-4786-b132-5ba65285b38c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <exercise id="_8b2410d3-bb2b-4626-b7a5-1bd9f96a758a" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Here is a graph representing <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00003">A rocket is launched in the air and its height, in feet, is modeled by the function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00004">
            <media alt="A curve on a graph, origin O, with grid. Horizontal axis, time, seconds, scale 0 to 8, by 1’s. Vertical axis, height, feet, scale 0 to 200, by 20’s. A curve passes through the points 0 comma 5, 3 comma 161, and 5 comma 105.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_07_10_01.svg"/>
            </media>
          </para>
          <para id="para-00005"><emphasis>Select three</emphasis> true statements about the situation.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00006">Correct! The rocket is launched from a height less than 20 feet above the ground. The rocket reaches its maximum height after about 3 seconds. The maximum height of the rocket is about 160 feet. </para>
          <para id="para-00007">Try again. Revisit activity 7.5.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00008">The correct answers are: The rocket is launched from a height less than 20 feet above the ground. The rocket reaches its maximum height after about 3 seconds. The maximum height of the rocket is about 160 feet.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="a7039bb0-885d-4513-8561-5888c03fbf04" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00009">Use this table to answer questions a–g.</para>
          <para id="para-00010">A baseball travels <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> meters <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> seconds after being dropped from the top of a building. The distance traveled by the baseball can be modeled by the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <table class="unnumbered os-raise-skinnytable" id="table-00001">
            <tgroup cols="2">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> (seconds) </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> (meters) </emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 0 </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 0.5 </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 1 </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 1.5 </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 2 </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
          <para id="para-00011">How many meters <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> did the baseball travel in 0 seconds <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00012">Correct! 0. The baseball traveled 0 meters <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> in 0 seconds <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> because it has not been dropped yet. </para>
          <para id="para-00013">Try again. Revisit activities 7.5.2 and 7.5.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00014">The correct answer is: 0. The baseball traveled 0 meters <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> in 0 seconds <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> because it has not been dropped yet.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="d8614f9a-5498-4ad9-ad3b-f24715e8b6a3" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00015">How many meters <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>) did the baseball travel in 0.5 seconds (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>)?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00016">Correct! 1.25. The baseball traveled 1.25 meters (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>) in 0.5 seconds (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>). </para>
          <para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activities 7.5.2 and 7.5.3. </para>
          <para id="para-00018">The correct answer is: 1.25. The baseball traveled 1.25 meters (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>) in 0.5 seconds (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="e8242ed2-1431-4717-91b8-338331d497fd" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00019">How many meters (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>) did the baseball travel in 1 second (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>)?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00020">Correct! 5. The baseball traveled 5 meters <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> in 1 second <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. </para>
          <para id="para-00021">Try again. Revisit activities 7.5.2 and 7.5.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00022">The correct answer is: 5. The baseball traveled 5 meters <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mi>\</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in 1 second <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_385149f7-7acb-405a-b608-184a5306e8b7" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00023">How many meters (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>) did the baseball travel in 1.5 seconds (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>)?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00024">Correct! 11.25. The baseball traveled 11.25 meters <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> in 1.5 seconds <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00025">Try again. Revisit activities 7.5.2 and 7.5.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00026">The correct answer is: 11.25. The baseball traveled 11.25 meters <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>\) in 1.5 seconds <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_29525aa0-e9f1-4f81-a7c4-de5b8d7d594d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00027">How many meters (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>) did the baseball travel in 2 seconds (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>)?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00028">Correct! 20. The baseball traveled 20 meters (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>) in 2 seconds (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>).</para>
          <para id="para-00029">Try again. Revisit activities 7.5.2 and 7.5.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00030">The correct answer is: 20. The baseball traveled 20 meters (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>d</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>) in 2 seconds (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="f86a8f64-56ea-4033-a2ec-5dc9a9dbad6f" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00031">Is this graph an accurate representation of the data in the table?  (<media alt="Insert Alt Text">
              <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_07_10_02.jpg"/>
            </media>)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00032">Correct! Yes. The coordinates plotted on the graph match the data in the table: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1.25</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>11.25</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00033">Try again. Revisit activities 7.5.2 and 7.5.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00034">The correct answer is: Yes. The coordinates plotted on the graph match the data in the table: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1.25</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>11.25</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_7cdcd3e2-4763-4178-9234-595a52e0abf9" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00035">Is the baseball traveling at a constant speed?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00036">Correct! The distance traveled is not changing at a constant speed; it is increasing over time. For example, in the first half second, it travels 1.25 meters, and in the next half second, it travels 3.75 meters.</para>
          <para id="para-00037">Try again. Revisit activities 7.5.2 and 7.5.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00038">The correct answer is: No. The distance traveled is not changing at a constant speed; it is increasing over time. For example, in the first half second, it travels 1.25 meters, and in the next half second, it travels 3.75 meters.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="aa57ecbc-5dbb-43a0-aaa7-3ef042f52830" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00039">A small ball is dropped from a 100-foot-tall building. Which equation could represent the ball’s height, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, in feet, relative to the ground, as a function of time, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, in seconds?</para>
          <para id="para-00040">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00041"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00042"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00043"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00044"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00045">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00046">Try again. Revisit activity 7.5.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00047">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>. </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
